message: >-
  If you use the OCN-1 catalogue or specification, please cite it as below
  (CC-BY-4.0 requires attribution; this is the canonical form).
title: "OCN — Open Chess Naming (OCN-1 specification and catalogue)"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Club d'Escacs Figueres"
    city: Figueres
    country: ES
repository-code: "https://github.com/escacsfigueres/ocn"
url: "https://github.com/escacsfigueres/ocn"
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-06-11
keywords:
  - chess
  - chess openings
  - ECO
  - naming scheme
  - dataset
abstract: >-
  OCN-1 is a hierarchical, human-readable naming scheme for chess openings,
  designed as a companion to ECO. The reference catalogue names 5,899
  opening families, variations and tabiyas with parent-aware slugs,
  position-identity relations (transposes_to, same_as) and sourced naming
  attributions. Code in tools/ is MIT-licensed; the specification and
  catalogue are CC-BY-4.0.
